{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 276372, "name": "adewart", "username": "adewart", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-16T11:48:34.571Z", "cooked": "<p>here’s the problem: by default the libs in fedora for playing videos produce a bad experience on asahi. mpv, vlc too skip frames, have trouble sync’ing after lots of fast forward and rewind events. i did find out that if i install the nonfree ffmpeg , nonfree codecs, and multimedia packages from rpmfusion, then playing videos with mpv was nice again. so far so good.</p>\n<p>then i wanted to compile rpcs3, now that we have opengl4.6.<br>\nbut then there was a chicken and egg problem, rpcs3 complained it couldn’t find some devel libs it needed, and if i tried to install those, then i saw i had a package conflict between rpmfusion and normal fedora repos. typically while attempting to compile rpcs3 i saw this:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">CMake Error at buildfiles/cmake/FindFFMPEG.cmake:90 (message):\n  Could not find libavcodec or libavformat or libavutil or libswscale or\n  libswresample\n</code></pre>\n<p>but if i tried to install libavcodec-free-devel (and some other libs too) i had dnf refusing to comply because of conflict. it suggested i use <code>--allowerasing</code> like so:</p>\n<p><code>sudo dnf install libavcodec-free-devel --allowerasing </code><br>\nso dnf said it would remove <code>ffmpeg-libs</code>  (and probably lots of other things to which i said yes …) and that immediately killed my kde session and left me with a broken install i had to fix by hand. so i have 1 problem to ask for help and eventualy one warning to share with others.</p>\n<p>the warning is : it seems rpmfusion doesn’t play nice with fedora39, there are packages conflicts… beware.</p>\n<p>the question is: how can i have a smooth video playback on fedora39 (using mpv) without using rpmfusion ?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-16T12:27:08.588Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 879, "reads": 34, "readers_count": 33, "score": 4401.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "adewart", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18476, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276565, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T08:12:20.194Z", "cooked": "<p>Did you try installing ffmpeg-devel?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"105251\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/eb7434/48.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/unable-to-install-dependencies-required-by-darlinghq/105251/2\">Unable to install dependencies required by darlinghq</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ask/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #38BC3B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category \" title=\"Have questions? Get answers here! Ask anything about installing, using, troubleshooting, customizing, or upgrading any variant of Fedora Linux.\"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">Ask Fedora</span></span></a>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    Because you’re using ffmpeg-libs from RPM Fusion in place of libavcodec-free et al., you need to install ffmpeg-devel instead of libavcodec-free-devel and libavformat-free-devel.\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T08:12:20.194Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 27, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 146.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/unable-to-install-dependencies-required-by-darlinghq/105251/2", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Unable to install dependencies required by darlinghq", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276601, "name": "adewart", "username": "adewart", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T12:09:37.388Z", "cooked": "<p>thank you for the reply. that could well be what i was missing.<br>\nsince rpcs3 asked specificaly for libavcodec, i searched for that string specificaly with dnf, but in rpmfusion the lib i needed could have been in that package. the name is a bit misleading. maybe i should have searched with <code>dnf provides */libavcodec</code> and that would have shown me <code>ffmpeg-devel</code> indeed. (i’ve just tested it). maybe rpmfusion should package those in the same way base fedora does, like: <code>libavcodec-non-free-devel</code> and so on for the rest of them. instead of putting it in a <code>ffmpeg-devel</code> that encapsulate them.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T12:10:00.188Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 35.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "adewart", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 638, "username": "grumpey", "name": "Joe Walker", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18476, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276625, "name": "Leif Liddy", "username": "leifliddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T14:13:03.350Z", "cooked": "<p>This might help:<br>\n<a href=\"https://rpmfusion.org/Howto/Multimedia\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://rpmfusion.org/Howto/Multimedia</a></p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T14:13:03.350Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 15.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "Leif Liddy", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://rpmfusion.org/Howto/Multimedia", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Howto/Multimedia - RPM Fusion", "clicks": 30}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16436, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276634, "name": "adewart", "username": "adewart", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T15:30:54.648Z", "cooked": "<p>that’s what i followed to install rpmfusion aand the multimedia libs and codecs. the problem was not installing them. the problem was naming convention and packaging unusual decision. as i mentionned above,<br>\ni was trying to compile rpcs3, which complained it wanted a specific dev lib. what is the normal reaction to that ?<br>\n<code>dnf search &lt;lib rpcs3 wanted&gt;</code> (in that case it was libavcodec). but rpmfusion decided to pack it among other libs into a package called “ffmpeg-libs”… how was i supposed to get the hint about that ? rpmfusion has a bad idea doing that. it should have followed the more traditional ‘libavcodec-nonfree’ naming scheme, or create a group ‘ffmpeg-libs’ yes… but a package encapsulating many libs under a loosely connected name ‘ffmpeg-libs’ ? i don’t think so.<br>\nhow the user will know what he need is encapsulated in there ? there is a workaround using <code>dnf provides */mylib</code> (as <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/grumpey\">@grumpey</a> mentionned) but all that is unorthodox. since package manager exists, the basic idea is : <code>package-manager search  stuff</code> command. and you get returned the name of the package for ‘stuff’ and not package name for ‘something else loosely related’.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T15:34:45.839Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 24.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "adewart", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 16436, "username": "leifliddy", "name": "Leif Liddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18476, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 638, "username": "grumpey", "name": "Joe Walker", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png"}], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276640, "name": "Leif Liddy", "username": "leifliddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T15:57:37.603Z", "cooked": "<p>I would just build rpcs3 in a container.<br>\nI just created a project that does that</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/2X/b/bad3e5f9ad67c1ddf145107ce7032ac1d7b22563.svg\" class=\"site-icon\" data-dominant-color=\"\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/344;\"><img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/optimized/3X/0/f/0ffc0418f78943517b155b74dae88c447cb4a204_2_690x345.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" data-dominant-color=\"F2F4F5\" width=\"690\" height=\"345\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub - leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder: builds rpcs3 to run on Fedora</a></h3>\n\n  <p>builds rpcs3 to run on Fedora. Contribute to leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder development by creating an account on GitHub.</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>If you try it out – let me know if you have any improvement suggestions for the build script</p><aside class=\"onebox githubblob\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">github.com</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <h4><a href=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh</a></h4>\n\n\n      <pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">#!/bin/bash\n\nset -e\n\nrpcs3_dir='/root/rpcs3'\nrpcs3_git_url='https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3'\narch=$(arch)\n\nwhile getopts :r arg\ndo\n    case \"${arg}\" in\n        r) rebuild=true ;;\n    esac\ndone\n\n[[ $rebuild = true ]] &amp;&amp; [[ -d $rpcs3_dir ]] &amp;&amp; rm -rf $rpcs3_dir\n[[ ! -d $rpcs3_dir ]] &amp;&amp; mkdir $rpcs3_dir &amp;&amp; rebuild=true\n\n[[ $rebuild = true ]] &amp;&amp; git clone --recursive $rpcs3_git_url $rpcs3_dir\n\n</code></pre>\n\n\n\n  This file has been truncated. <a href=\"https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">show original</a>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T15:57:37.603Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 9, "reads": 22, "readers_count": 21, "score": 49.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "Leif Liddy", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "GitHub - leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder: builds rpcs3 to run on Fedora", "clicks": 20}, {"url": "https://github.com/leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder/blob/main/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "podman-rpcs3-builder/build.scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh at main · leifliddy/podman-rpcs3-builder · GitHub", "clicks": 11}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16436, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276643, "name": "Leif Liddy", "username": "leifliddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T16:04:28.746Z", "cooked": "<p>The whole thing is pretty confusing. The rpmfusion devs were not happy at all that Fedora released these “free” versions of ffmpeg, libavformat…etc<br>\nAs they’re simply subsets of the full packages that rpmfusion offers.<br>\nI think there should have been a vote on it – instead of just throwing a monkey wrench into the whole thing.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T16:04:28.746Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 19, "readers_count": 18, "score": 13.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "Leif Liddy", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16436, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "totally", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276652, "name": "adewart", "username": "adewart", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-17T16:41:04.376Z", "cooked": "<p>interesting. i will look at that container script.<br>\nthank you for telling and also for letting me know i’m not alone thinking this issue about packaging was confusing.</p>\n<p>actually, looking at your script, is it not just automating the compilation ? will it not still require necessary libs to get installed ? if so that bring us back to similar case. what is that “container” thing you’ve mentioned ? is that some sort of portable, standalone build ?</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-17T16:51:24.885Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 7, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 20, "readers_count": 19, "score": 24.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "adewart", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 16436, "username": "leifliddy", "name": "Leif Liddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18476, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3/105392/8", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 276824, "name": "Leif Liddy", "username": "leifliddy", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/b193c8/{size}.png", "created_at": "2024-02-18T11:00:24.785Z", "cooked": "<p>So rpcs3 only has a built-in submodule for x86_64 for ffmpeg some reason.<br>\nSo I wasn’t sure if I should compile it for aarch64 with the full (rpmfusion) ffmpeg package or not.<br>\nIn the end I just used the rpmfusion package just to be sure. But I see your point – that sort brings us full circle. Since I can’t manage to Tekken TT2 to fully load on my macbook m1 air (it’s the only game I have) – I can’t how rpcs3 performs.</p>\n<p>So how the project works is that it uses the podman api to automate the creation of the podman image (rpcs3_build_env) and the podman container (rpcs3_builder)</p>\n<p>Running ./script-podman.py will build the image + container + then run the container.</p>\n<p>You then enter the container env with<br>\npodman exec -it rpcs3_builder /bin/bash</p>\n<p>from there you just run /root/scripts/01-build.rpcs3.sh<br>\nto build rpcs3.</p>", "post_number": 9, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2024-02-18T11:00:24.785Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 8, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 16, "readers_count": 15, "score": 18.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 105392, "topic_slug": "rpmfusion-and-compiling-rpcs3", "display_username": "Leif Liddy", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 18476, "username": "adewart", "name": "adewart", "avata